      "id": "decl-sweep-2x2",
      "name": "The 2x2 declarative sweep, end to end",
      "description": "The main event: smoke test, generate all four cells, train the 2x2 comparison, score the companion thresholds. One button, about four and a half hours, no parameters -- every path in it is a literal. It regenerates the four cells every time, even when they are already on disk, which costs about 25 minutes and buys an entry with no hidden prerequisite; generation is deterministic, so it rewrites the same bytes. If the cells are already there and only the training needs repeating -- a comparison that failed at hour three, say -- use 'Declarative sweep: compare the four cells' instead.",
